e2e/demo-videos/

# Deployment secrets. docker-compose.yml AUTOMATICALLY reads the .env sitting next to it for its
# ${...} substitutions — that is where BETTER_AUTH_SECRET and CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY live.
# backend/ and frontend/ already ignore their own .env in their own .gitignore; the repository root
# did not, so a `git add -A` would have published the deployment's secret file.
# .env.example is the template, values blank: that one stays versioned.
# Patterns are root-anchored (leading "/"): backend/.env.test and frontend/.env.test are tracked and
# must stay so, and an unanchored pattern would match them too.
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example

# Launch video workspace (generated, not part of the product)
brag-output/

# Liste personnelle du mandant — suivie hors dépôt
TODO_MANDANT.md

# Planning and audit notes. These describe what is not done yet, what was found and not yet fixed,
# and when each thing is due — the kind of writing that is honest precisely because nobody outside
# is reading it. Published on a public repository it becomes a map of the gaps, and one of these
# named an unpublished security advisory as affecting the released line. They stay on disk and out
# of git; TODO_MANDANT.md was already here for the same reason.
AUDIT_VALIDATION.md
MIGRATION_SOURCES.md
RELEASE_PLAN.md
TODO_FEATURES.md

# Same reasoning, one level down: the internal decision log records arbitrations that were made in
# the open with the owner, including the ones that were reversed. It is a working record, not a
# statement of what the product does — the data files carry that, each with its own sources.
documentation/internal/DECISIONS.md
documentation/internal/audit/
